# Rent Is Due: with only one untapped creature or Treasure there is nothing to tap two of, so "otherwise" applies with no question asked.
# Bot1 has one Ornithopter, an untapped Plains and Mox Pearl (neither a creature nor a Treasure): Rent Is Due is sacrificed and nothing is
# drawn. There is no question to Accept (the refusal line), so a miscount that asked "you may" would fail it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Rent Is Due
Mox Pearl
Ornithopter
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rent Is Due.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T1 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Rent Is Due = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Stack.Count = 0
